abstract: >-
  PathQ-Former reads whole-slide-image patch embeddings and RNA-seq pathway tokens through two banks of
  learned queries, fuses the codes with a small Transformer and predicts discrete-time survival hazards.
  Absent modalities are replaced by learned null codes, so one checkpoint serves WSI+RNA, WSI-only and
  RNA-only patients. Under an identical fixed-budget protocol on five TCGA cohorts it improves the C-index
  over the official SurvPath implementation by +0.037 pooled over 75 paired folds (p = 0.002) while keeping
  0.54-0.67 with either modality removed.
